            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\n> it doesn't seem gracefully handle creating a snippet, and then choosing to delete it.\n\nThis is an expected and documented behavior, as [editing text within snippet range but outside of snippet lifecycle is not supported](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/be81509b7160aa02264a59789164a2e1c4a6750a/doc/mini-snippets.txt#L1118-L1123). Specifically for the reason described in this issue, as there is no clear way to fix this without causing problems somewhere else. This was also described in #1703.\n\nThe assumed approach is to [explicitly stop](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/be81509b7160aa02264a59789164a2e1c4a6750a/doc/mini-snippets.txt#L1102-L1103) the snippet session when it is not needed. This works both before and after this not supported text edit in Normal mode.",
